@startuml
title Architecture overview
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Clients" as Clients {
  actor "Alice\n(client)" as Alice
  actor "Bob\n(client)" as Bob
  actor "Mallory\n(attacker, ordinary client)" as Mallory
}

component "Relay Server" as Server
database "DB" as DB

Clients -right-> Server : HTTP\nregister, get_key, send
Server .left.> Clients : WebSocket\nbroadcast feed
Server -right-> DB : store / read

note bottom of Clients
  **Client responsibilities**
  - generate and persist own RSA key pair
    (private key never leaves the device)
  - encrypt / decrypt, sign / verify
  - keep a local copy of own sent plaintext
  - apply receive logic: check "to", verify
    signature, decrypt, parse payload
  - on parse failure, send the error bounce
    (the deliberate oracle)

  Mallory is a registered user like anyone else:
  same HTTP access, same broadcast feed.
  No special network position is assumed or needed.
end note

note bottom of Server
  **Server responsibilities**
  - key directory: first-come, no overwrite
  - accept frames via POST /messages,
    check size / JSON shape only
  - store every frame verbatim
  - broadcast every frame to all open sockets
  - never parses ciphertext or signatures,
    never decides who is right or wrong
end note

note bottom of DB
  **Storage responsibilities**
  - "keys": name -> public_key (PK, no overwrite)
  - "messages": log of raw frames,
    extra columns for human-readable filtering only
  - never queried by the server itself
end note
@enduml
